---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StickyConsultationCTA from '../components/StickyConsultationCTA.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CalEmbed from '../components/CalEmbed.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

// ── Imagery (every slot a distinct image; warm-graded into one coherent set) ──
import moonlitShore from '../assets/moonlit-shore-meditation.jpg'; // hero: dark anchor
import forestPath from '../assets/mysterious-forest-path.JPG';   // break 01: light
import majesticHills from '../assets/majestic-landscape-hills-and-clouds.JPG'; // break 02: light
import mountainDusk from '../assets/mountain-dusk-vista.jpg';     // break 03: dark anchor
import mistyRidge from '../assets/misty-mountain-ridge.jpg';      // break 04: light
import himalayaSnowPeak from '../assets/himalaya-snow-peak.jpg'; // break 05: light
import ramaRooftop from '../assets/Rama-silhoute-in-yoga-hall.PNG'; // break 06: light
import michaelPortrait from '../assets/michael-portrait-new.jpg'; // hero portrait
import veraPortrait from '../assets/Vera-Pic.PNG';
import ashrafPortrait from '../assets/Ashraf-pic.jpg';
import bernardPortrait from '../assets/bernard-altman-portrait.jpg';

const canonicalURL = 'https://www.sangham.org/counselling-for-meditators/';
const WHATSAPP = 'https://wa.me/27736738063';
const EMAIL = 'ramarishi@sangham.org';

// ── "A different way of looking": four lenses (tabbed) ──
const lenses = [
  {
    tab: 'The body',
    lead: 'Through the body',
    body: 'Intensive practice changes the nervous system. A shift like this can have a real physiological dimension: how you are sleeping, breathing, eating, and regulating energy all shape what arises and how stable it feels.',
  },
  {
    tab: 'The psyche',
    lead: 'Through the psyche',
    body: 'An experience like this often touches personal history: what the loss of a familiar self-sense stirs up, the fear or relief it brings, and the meaning you find yourself reaching for.',
  },
  {
    tab: 'Relationships & culture',
    lead: 'Through relationships and culture',
    body: 'How an experience lands depends partly on the people around you and the language your background gives you. The same event can feel isolating in one setting and intelligible in another.',
  },
  {
    tab: 'Contemplative tradition',
    lead: 'Through contemplative tradition',
    body: 'Many traditions have described states like this for centuries, with detailed maps of what they are, how they move, and how to relate to them. That lineage can offer real context, though it is not the only valid one.',
  },
];

// ── About Michael: four panels (tabbed; all labels visible) ──
const michaelPanels = [
  {
    title: 'Facilitation and counselling',
    paras: [
      'For 10+ years I have worked in and around human development, transformation, and self-understanding: facilitating group processes, supporting people through periods of significant change, and working with questions of identity, meaning, purpose, and relationship.',
      'My background is in psychology and counselling. But the question that has always interested me most sits underneath both: how do we come to understand ourselves more honestly?',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Contemplative practice',
    paras: [
      'For more than eight years, contemplative practice has been at the centre of my life. That has meant extended silent retreats, long periods of solitude, traditional training in India, and immersion in contemplative communities and ways of living.',
      'Much of that time has gone into questions that sit awkwardly in either psychological or spiritual categories: awareness, suffering, identity, and what remains when our ordinary assumptions about ourselves begin to loosen. I mention it only because it is part of the ground I work from. Much of what people bring to these conversations is not abstract to me.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Where psychology and spirituality meet',
    paras: [
      'One thing the years have taught me is that neither psychology nor spirituality, on its own, captures the whole of a human life. Psychology offers real insight, language, and support. The contemplative traditions offer context, depth, and the reassurance of others who have walked similar paths. Both matter. Both also narrow things when treated as the only valid lens. Much of my work lives in the conversation between them.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'How I work',
    paras: [
      "I don't see my role as handing over answers, diagnoses, or interpretations for you to adopt. More often it means listening closely, reflecting back what I hear, asking the questions that have not yet been asked, and helping you examine the stories and conclusions that have formed around your experience.",
      'Sometimes a new perspective emerges. Sometimes an old one deepens. Sometimes the most useful discovery is that a question needs more time before it can be answered honestly. Throughout, the work stays yours. My part is to help create the conditions in which your own understanding can come into focus.',
    ],
  },
];

// ── "What this work often meets": progressive-disclosure cards ──
const meetsCards = [
  { head: "Something happened in practice, and you don't know what to make of it.", body: 'An experience that felt important, beautiful, frightening, or all at once, and that you have had no way to place.' },
  { head: 'A retreat or a powerful insight has changed how you see your life.', body: 'Something opened, and now you are unsure what comes next, or how to live from it.' },
  { head: 'Your practice is affecting your relationships.', body: 'You are changing, or trying to share something that matters to you, and the people closest to you do not quite understand what is happening.' },
  { head: "There are energetic or bodily experiences you can't account for.", body: 'Changes in sleep, appetite, sexuality, perception, or mood, and you want to understand them without either dismissing or inflating them.' },
  { head: 'You feel caught between explanations.', body: 'One teacher says one thing, another says the opposite, psychology says something else, and your own experience seems to say something else again.' },
  { head: 'There is a quiet fear that something is wrong with you.', body: 'Or the opposite fear: that something important is happening, and you might lose contact with it.' },
  { head: 'You feel alone in it.', body: 'Not for lack of people around you, but because there is no one you can speak to honestly about what you are living through.' },
  { head: 'There is no dramatic experience at all.', body: 'Only a sense that practice has brought you somewhere the old answers no longer reach, and you are unsure of the next step.' },
];

// ── Reflections ──
const reflections = [
  { img: veraPortrait, pos: 'object-[center_30%]', label: 'Personal Reflection', name: 'Vera', role: 'Workshop participant', quote: 'Michael is a truly special person. Beyond the depth of wisdom and knowledge he shares, there is something deeply healing about his presence. During the workshop, I found myself softening, opening, and gently meeting parts of myself I had long found difficult to face. He holds space with a rare combination of patience, authenticity, and humility, making it easy to feel safe and fully present with oneself. I left feeling more connected to myself, and deeply grateful for the experience.' },
  { img: ashrafPortrait, pos: 'object-[40%_center]', label: 'Personal Reflection', name: 'Ashraf Vahed', role: 'Has known Michael through community work', quote: 'It is a rare thing to encounter so much wisdom in one person. In my time with Michael, I have experienced a peace that only comes with deep trust: of being held without judgement, in a field of infinite compassion. I have felt my best parts come forward, and a relatability to all sides of humanity, expressed with love and equanimity. It is rare for me to give so easily to the guidance of a man, and rare to find one with such a capacity to guide.' },
  { img: bernardPortrait, pos: 'object-[center_25%]', label: 'Professional Reflection', name: 'Bernard Altman', role: 'Clinical Psychologist', quote: 'He brings presence, emotional intelligence, and a strong capacity to engage honestly with difficult human experiences. I would recommend him with confidence.' },
];

// ── FAQ ──
const faqItems = [
  { q: 'Is this therapy?', a: 'No. This is reflective counselling rather than psychotherapy or clinical treatment. Psychological insight and emotional exploration are often part of the conversation, but the primary focus is helping people understand and integrate experiences arising through spiritual practice and inner development.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to belong to a particular tradition?', a: 'No. People come from many different backgrounds and practices, including meditation, yoga, contemplative Christianity, Buddhism, non-dual traditions, devotional paths, and sometimes no formal tradition at all. What matters is not which path you are on, but whether you want to understand your experience more deeply.' },
  { q: 'Will you tell me what my experiences mean?', a: 'No. My role is not to provide definitive interpretations. The work involves exploring experiences together, questioning assumptions, considering different perspectives, and making space for your own understanding to emerge.' },
  { q: "What if I'm not sure whether this is right for me?", a: 'That uncertainty is completely fine. The free 15-minute fit call exists precisely so we can look at what is happening, whether this work is likely to help, and whether we feel like a good fit to work together. There is no obligation to continue.' },
  { q: 'How do sessions work?', a: 'Sessions take place online by video call. The work is conversational rather than curriculum-based. Some people come with a specific experience to explore; others arrive with broader questions about practice, direction, relationships, or meaning. The pace and focus follow what you are actually living through, not a predetermined programme.' },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: item.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a } })),
};

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Counselling for Meditators and Contemplative Practitioners',
    url: canonicalURL,
    description: 'Reflective counselling for people exploring consciousness in meaningful ways. A grounded space to understand what your practice and experiences may be opening, with someone who has spent years in similar terrain. ASCHP registered. Online worldwide.',
    serviceType: 'Wellness Counselling',
    provider: {
      '@type': 'Person',
      name: 'Michael Kaplan',
      alternateName: 'Swami Ramarishi',
      jobTitle: 'ASCHP Registered Wellness Counsellor',
      url: 'https://www.sangham.org/about',
      sameAs: ['https://www.instagram.com/sangham.space'],
      hasCredential: {
        '@type': 'EducationalOccupationalCredential',
        credentialCategory: 'Professional Registration',
        name: 'Wellness Counsellor',
        recognizedBy: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Association for Supportive Counsellors and Holistic Practitioners', alternateName: 'ASCHP' },
        identifier: 'Reg. No. 10559',
      },
      affiliation: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Association for Supportive Counsellors and Holistic Practitioners', alternateName: 'ASCHP' },
    },
    areaServed: [{ '@type': 'Country', name: 'South Africa' }, { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Worldwide' }],
    availableChannel: { '@type': 'ServiceChannel', serviceType: 'Online via video call', availableLanguage: 'English' },
    offers: [
      { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'Free 15-Minute Fit Call', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'ZAR', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock', description: 'A free 15-minute call to understand what is happening and whether this work is a good fit. No obligation to continue.' },
      { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'Ongoing Session', price: '850', priceCurrency: 'ZAR', availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock', description: '60-minute reflective counselling session, online via video.' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<style is:global>
  .cfm {
    --cfm-cream: hsl(36 18% 88%);
    --cfm-warm: hsl(38 30% 84%);
    --cfm-gold: hsl(41 48% 31%);        /* large headings & links on light: ~4.7:1 on cream */
    --cfm-gold-deep: hsl(40 52% 26%);   /* small labels on light: ~5.3:1 on cream/warm */
    --cfm-gold-light: hsl(42 54% 57%);  /* gold on deep navy: ~5.6:1, safe for small text */
    --cfm-ink: hsl(30 12% 20%);
    --cfm-navy: hsl(220 22% 12%);
    --cfm-navy-deep: hsl(220 26% 8%);
    --cfm-parch: hsl(36 22% 86%);
  }
  .cfm-warm-bg { background-color: var(--cfm-warm); }

  /* Deep anchor sections: light text on navy, used for the most charged moments */
  .cfm-dark { background-color: var(--cfm-navy); color: var(--cfm-parch); }
  .cfm-dark-deep { background-color: var(--cfm-navy-deep); color: var(--cfm-parch); }
  .cfm-dark p, .cfm-dark li { color: hsl(36 20% 86% / 0.84); }
  .cfm-dark .cfm-emph { color: hsl(36 24% 92%); }

  .cfm-gold-text { color: var(--cfm-gold); }
  .cfm-gold-deep-text { color: var(--cfm-gold-deep); }
  .cfm-gold-light-text { color: var(--cfm-gold-light); }
  .cfm-rule { height: 1px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--cfm-gold), transparent); opacity: 0.5; }
  .cfm-rule-light { height: 1px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--cfm-gold-light), transparent); opacity: 0.55; }

  /* Pull-quote over a LIGHT break: ink serif on a strong cream scrim: bulletproof contrast */
  .cfm-quote { color: hsl(30 14% 18%); text-shadow: 0 1px 16px hsl(36 30% 96% / 0.6); }
  /* Pull-quote over a DARK break: warm gold serif glowing on a navy scrim */
  .cfm-quote-dark { color: var(--cfm-gold-light); text-shadow: 0 2px 30px hsl(220 30% 4% / 0.6); }

  /* Warm, consistent grade so the sunset, snow, misty and moonlit shots read as one set */
  .cfm-graded img { filter: saturate(0.95) brightness(1.02) contrast(0.99) sepia(0.07); }
  .cfm-graded-dark img { filter: saturate(0.9) brightness(0.92) contrast(1.04) sepia(0.06); }

  /* Underline-grow links */
  .cfm-link {
    background-image: linear-gradient(currentColor, currentColor);
    background-size: 0% 1px; background-repeat: no-repeat; background-position: 0 100%;
    transition: background-size 0.3s ease; padding-bottom: 1px;
  }
  .cfm-link:hover, .cfm-link:focus-visible { background-size: 100% 1px; }

  /* Reveal on scroll */
  .cfm-reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(24px); transition: opacity 0.6s ease-out, transform 0.6s ease-out; }
  .cfm-reveal.cfm-in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }

  /* Slow ken-burns on full-bleed images */
  .cfm-kb-img { animation: cfmKb 26s ease-in-out infinite alternate; transform-origin: center; will-change: transform; }
  @keyframes cfmKb { from { transform: scale(1.03); } to { transform: scale(1.11); } }

  /* Tabs */
  .cfm-tab { transition: color 0.25s ease, border-color 0.25s ease, background-color 0.25s ease; }
  .cfm-tabpanel[hidden] { display: none; }
  .cfm-tabpanel { animation: cfmFade 0.35s ease; }
  @keyframes cfmFade { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }

  /* Progressive-disclosure card body */
  .cfm-card > .cfm-card-body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: 0fr; transition: grid-template-rows 0.3s ease; }
  .cfm-card[open] > .cfm-card-body { grid-template-rows: 1fr; }
  .cfm-card > .cfm-card-body > div { overflow: hidden; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cfm-reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    .cfm-kb-img { animation: none !important; }
    .cfm-tabpanel { animation: none !important; }
    .cfm-card > .cfm-card-body { transition: none !important; }
  }
</style>

<BaseLayout
  title="Counselling for Meditators"
  description="A grounded counselling space for people making sense of what meditation or contemplative practice may be opening. Online worldwide."
  canonicalURL={canonicalURL}
  image="/images/og-counselling-for-meditators.jpg"
  jsonLd={[...jsonLd, faqJsonLd]}
  hideStickyBar={true}
>
<div class="cfm bg-background text-foreground">

  <!-- ═══ 01 · HERO: deep anchor (moonlit shore) ═══ -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden -mt-[72px] pt-[72px] cfm-dark-deep">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 cfm-graded-dark">
      <Image src={moonlitShore} alt="" aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-[center_38%] cfm-kb-img" widths={[768, 1280, 1600]} quality={72} sizes="100vw" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
    <!-- Legibility scrim: dense on the text (left) side, opening to the moonlit sky on the right -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0" style="background: linear-gradient(100deg, hsl(220 26% 8% / 0.96) 0%, hsl(220 26% 8% / 0.9) 38%, hsl(220 26% 8% / 0.66) 66%, hsl(220 26% 8% / 0.42) 100%);"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0" style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, hsl(220 26% 8% / 0.55) 0%, transparent 22%, transparent 72%, hsl(220 26% 8% / 0.6) 100%);"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 lg:py-32 max-w-5xl">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-parchment/55 text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase font-body mb-8">
            South African-registered &middot; Currently based in India &middot; Online worldwide
          </p>
          <h1 class="font-heading text-gold-gradient text-[34px] sm:text-5xl md:text-[54px] lg:text-[62px] leading-[1.1] mb-9">
            <span class="block mb-3">Meditation can open profound questions.</span>
            <span class="block">You do not have to navigate them alone.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="font-body text-lg md:text-xl text-parchment/82 leading-relaxed mb-9 max-w-xl">
            A reflective counselling space for people exploring consciousness in meaningful ways. Somewhere to make sense of what your practice and experiences may be opening, with someone who has spent years in similar terrain.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 mb-3">
            <a href="#cal-inline-embed" data-cta="book-fit-call" data-service="meditators" data-placement="hero" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-8 py-4 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-gold-light hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 rounded-lg text-sm tracking-wider uppercase font-body font-medium shadow-lg shadow-black/25">
              Book a free 15-minute fit call
            </a>
            <a href={WHATSAPP} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-cta="whatsapp" data-channel="whatsapp" data-service="meditators" data-placement="hero" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-7 py-4 border border-parchment/30 text-parchment/85 hover:border-gold-light hover:text-gold-light hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 rounded-lg text-sm tracking-wide font-body">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413z"/></svg>
              Message on WhatsApp
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="font-body text-sm italic text-parchment/55 mb-8">Unhurried, and free. No obligation to continue.</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
            {['ASCHP Registered Wellness Counsellor', 'BA Psychology', 'Certified Yoga Teacher (RYS 300)', 'Online Worldwide'].map((t) => (
              <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-gold-light/30 text-parchment/75 text-[11px] font-body bg-white/[0.04]">{t}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex justify-center md:justify-end">
          <div class="w-full max-w-[230px] lg:max-w-[250px]">
            <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-parchment/15 shadow-xl shadow-black/30 cfm-graded">
              <div class="aspect-[4/5] overflow-hidden">
                <Image src={michaelPortrait} alt="Michael Kaplan (Swami Ramarishi), ASCHP Registered Wellness Counsellor" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" widths={[400, 500]} sizes="250px" width={1254} height={1254} loading="eager" />
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="font-heading text-base text-parchment/90 mt-3">Michael Kaplan (Swami Ramarishi)</p>
            <p class="cfm-gold-light-text text-[11px] font-body tracking-wide mt-1 leading-snug">ASCHP Registered Wellness Counsellor (Reg. 10559) &middot; RYS 300</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 01b · EXPERIENTIAL CREDIBILITY: editorial pause between hero and reading ═══ -->
  <section class="cfm-warm-bg border-b border-border/50">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-14 md:py-20 max-w-5xl cfm-reveal">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-10 sm:gap-0 text-center sm:text-left sm:divide-x sm:divide-border/70">
        <div class="sm:pr-10 lg:pr-14">
          <p class="font-heading cfm-gold-text text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-[56px] leading-none mb-3">10+ Years</p>
          <p class="font-body text-[15px] text-foreground/70 leading-relaxed max-w-[26ch] mx-auto sm:mx-0">facilitating transformative and contemplative work</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm:px-10 lg:px-14">
          <p class="font-heading cfm-gold-text text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-[56px] leading-none mb-3">8+ Years</p>
          <p class="font-body text-[15px] text-foreground/70 leading-relaxed max-w-[26ch] mx-auto sm:mx-0">of dedicated contemplative practice across several traditions</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm:pl-10 lg:pl-14">
          <p class="font-heading cfm-gold-text text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] leading-tight mb-3">Extended Periods</p>
          <p class="font-body text-[15px] text-foreground/70 leading-relaxed max-w-[26ch] mx-auto sm:mx-0">of silence, solitude, retreat, and traditional training</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 02 · SOMETHING MANY PEOPLE ON THIS PATH COME TO KNOW ═══ -->
  <section class="bg-background">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-3xl cfm-reveal">
      <h2 class="font-heading cfm-gold-text text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] leading-tight mb-10">Something many people on this path come to know</h2>
      <p class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-[30px] text-foreground/90 leading-snug mb-10 max-w-[42rem]">There are experiences that arise through spiritual practice that turn out to be surprisingly hard to speak about.</p>
      <div class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/75 leading-relaxed space-y-7 max-w-[65ch]">
        <p>A period of unusual clarity, where everything feels simple and obvious, can give way to a period where you cannot find your footing at all. Questions about who you are refuse to settle. Something fundamental seems to have shifted, and parts of the life you built around an earlier version of yourself no longer fit in quite the same way.</p>
        <p>Old grief, fear, anger, or longing can surface with an intensity that seems out of all proportion to your present circumstances. Experiences in meditation, prayer, or solitude feel deeply significant and yet remain almost impossible to explain to the people around you. There are stretches of profound peace, and stretches of contraction and doubt. There can be powerful energetic phenomena, or changes in sleep, appetite, sexuality, perception, and the way you inhabit your own body. Some traditions would name parts of this Kundalini, awakening, non-duality, or grace.</p>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="my-12 md:my-14 border-l-2 border-primary/50 pl-7 md:pl-8">
        <p class="font-heading cfm-gold-text text-[26px] md:text-[32px] italic leading-snug max-w-[30ch]">Sometimes these experiences are beautiful. Sometimes they are frightening. Often they are both.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/75 leading-relaxed space-y-7 max-w-[65ch]">
        <p>What makes them harder still is that most people have no context for them. The people closest to you may be worried. Your family may not understand. Your therapist may never have encountered anything like it. And so you find yourself reading late into the night, trying to work out whether you are waking up, breaking down, or losing your mind.</p>
        <p>For most of history, experiences like these were held within traditions that had language for them, and people who had walked similar ground before. Whether that ground was always read wisely is another question. What mattered was that the experience sat inside some wider understanding. Today, many people meet the same territory almost entirely alone.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cfm-rule w-16 my-10 md:my-12"></div>

