  <!-- ═══ 06 · WHAT THIS IS ═══ -->
  <section class="bg-background">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-3xl cfm-reveal">
      <h2 class="font-heading cfm-gold-text text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] leading-tight mb-12">What this is</h2>
      <div class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/75 leading-relaxed space-y-7 max-w-[65ch] mb-14">
        <p>This is a reflective counselling relationship. At its simplest, it is a space to bring the questions, uncertainties, and insights that arise through spiritual practice into honest conversation.</p>
        <p>Sometimes that conversation is about a single experience. Sometimes it is about a period of life that no longer makes sense the way it once did. Sometimes it is about practice itself: what is helping, what is not, what feels clear, and what does not.</p>
        <p>The aim is not to reach conclusions as quickly as possible. It is to understand more fully what is actually happening.</p>
        <p class="text-foreground/90">The work draws on three strands.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-px mb-14">
        {[
          { n: '01', t: 'Reflective counselling', b: 'The foundation is dialogue. Together we look carefully at your experience: not only what is happening, but how you are relating to it, the meaning you are making of it, and the assumptions quietly shaping that meaning. This is held within my training and registration as a Wellness Counsellor through the ASCHP.' },
          { n: '02', t: 'Contemplative familiarity', b: 'Alongside it sits many years of personal practice, retreat, and traditional training, and direct acquaintance with the kinds of questions and difficulties that can emerge on an inner path. Not because my experience is the same as yours, but because some territory is easier to explore in the company of someone who has travelled through similar landscapes themselves.' },
          { n: '03', t: 'Your own clarity', b: 'The purpose of this work is not for you to adopt my beliefs or conclusions. It is not a guru-disciple relationship, and it is not a matter of being told what your experiences "really mean." The aim is for your own understanding to deepen, whether through questioning, through reflection, or through seeing something from an angle you had not considered. The goal is not dependence. The goal is clarity.' },
        ].map((s) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-5 md:gap-8 items-start border-t border-border/60 py-8">
